tidely: I'd have to dig deeper into the codebase, at least for someone new to the codebase I'm experiencing some weird behavior. `Point::new(Line(10), Column(10))` doesn't seem to panic, however `Point::new(Line(2), Column(10))` does? Both of these are outside of the 5 by 5 `Grid`
chrisduerr: That's an interesting case because `(2, 10)` is not actually *after* `self.end`. So you're passing an invalid position *before* the end of the grid iterator, which causes it to attempt to access a cell that doesn't exist.

Technically starting an iterator from an invalid point was never supported, I just suggested to add this since I know it works fine if the start is completely outside the grid anyway which applies to y our `(10, 10)` example.

That said, this is an issue we can actually easily fix without any performance penalty, so I suggest applying the following patch:

